Revision history for Mojolicious-Plugin-Buffer

0.001.0
	Initial version.
	Make the different-keys single-flight test independent of the order in
	which concurrent requests reach their actions.
	Fold the simulated no-HTML::Packer test into the hidden-module suite,
	including level 2 coverage.
	Test added, deleted and symlinked template directories, covering
	directory mtimes and symlink-loop protection.
	Add template_mtime_cache and template_mtime_cache_duration so the
	template tree scan can be cached, including across workers.
	Test cache hits, expiry, scan fallback and option validation.
	Benchmark the default template mtime scan against an explicit epoch
	on a 10,000-template tree and document the trade-off.
	Test a hypnotoad waiter receiving 503 when another worker holds the
	shared lock past cache_lock_timeout.
	Test that a hypnotoad worker killed while holding the shared lock
	releases it for the remaining workers.
	Assert that the concurrent cold requests used more than one worker
	pid, so cross-worker locking is actually exercised.
	Add a runnable hypnotoad example under eg/hypnotoad.
	Add an optional live Redis integration test, skipped unless
	MPB_REDIS_URL or REDIS_URL is configured.
	Audit the concurrency tests for completion-order assumptions: release
	the shared lock only once the waiter has joined, for the file, Redis and
	cross-process backends, and flush the cross-process handshake so a
	waiting request is not served from an entry filled before it arrived.
